WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.500
<v Jonas Brandt>Thanks for joining. Two items today: the T2 price and the rider survey.

2
00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:12.000
<v Carl Ekstrom>Before that, the Q3 close is signed off, so the numbers in the board pack match the ledger.

3
00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:18.000
<v Jonas Brandt>Good. On the price: I will publish the memo replacing 2,490 today.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:23.000
<v Carl Ekstrom>Fine by me. Will the old memo still be in the shared folder?

5
00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:28.500
<v Jonas Brandt>Yes, it stays as the cost step. The new memo is the one people should quote.

6
00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:34.000
<v Noor Haddad>Noor reports the rider survey result. Riders put the bike above our cost-plus price.

7
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:39.000
<v Jonas Brandt>That fits what I expected. Did the competitor band hold up when you checked it?

8
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:45.000
<v Noor Haddad>Yes, the comparable 720 Wh mid-drive bikes still sit in the same band. I put the source list in the sheet.

9
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:50.500
<v Carl Ekstrom>Does the survey change the cash plan at all?

10
00:00:50.500 --> 00:00:57.000
<v Noor Haddad>Only the timing of the first dealer orders. I will update the cash forecast once Sales confirms the order dates.

11
00:00:57.000 --> 00:01:02.000
<v Jonas Brandt>Good. Sales asked for one number for the briefing deck, so I want the memo out before that.

12
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:07.500
<v Carl Ekstrom>I can add the T2 line to the close checklist so the margin shows up in the November pack.

13
00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:12.000
<v Jonas Brandt>Please do. Anything else on pricing?

14
00:01:12.000 --> 00:01:17.000
<v Noor Haddad>No. Next sync is the budget review on the 28th, with the revenue sheet and the cost sheet.
